    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0112" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg104"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/1222: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-17T11:00:00-03:00">December 17,
                            1939—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 17—10:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>439. Department’s 237, December 16, 2 p.m. Cantilo is urgently requesting
                    Aranha’s support for his draft of protest to be made in connection with
                    Declaration of Panama. Aranha says in his opinion Cantilo’s note is satisfactory
                    but of course he wants to cooperate with us. Aranha is talking to President
                        Vargas<anchor n="30" xml:id="d136-f1"/> on whole subject early this
                    afternoon and will talk to me again later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d136-f1" n="30" xml:id="d136-f1-content">
                <p>Getulio Vargas, President of Brazil.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
